      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-119556",
      ":question/problem": "At a light show, the area of a square is being enlarged by $4%$ every second. The initial area of the square was $25cm^{2}$. Which of the following statements are true?\n\n1. The square's area is $25 \\cdot (1.04)^{4}$ square centimeters after $3$ seconds.\n2. The relationship between the time and the square's area is linear.\n3. The relationship between the time and the square's area is exponential.\n\n> A calculator is required to answer this question."
